### `mcp__codex_app__create_thread`
Create a separate task only when the user explicitly asks for a new task. The prompt appears as a user-visible message in the new task. Write clear, cohesive, human-readable prose. Use project for local or remote repository work, projectless for local work without a repository, or chatgptWorkCloud only when the user explicitly asks for a cloud work task in ChatGPT. Call list_projects before using project. Default to local; use worktree only when the user explicitly requests it and isGitRepository is true. Creation is non-blocking. A ready thread returns threadId and hostId; setup in progress may return clientThreadId, which must not be passed to tools that require threadId. This tool is part of plugin `codex-app-tools`.

